# Automatic custom-plan names

Generate numbered default names for newly created Cards and Constructions plans.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The first Cards plan defaults to `Card plan 1`.
- [x] The first Constructions plan defaults to `Con plan 1`.
- [x] If that name exists, the next new plan of the same kind receives the next available positive number.
- [x] Numbering is independent between Cards and Constructions plans.
- [x] Numbering is independent for each player because custom-plan collections belong to a player colour.
- [x] User-entered names remain editable and are never renamed after Save.
- [x] Cancelling creation does not consume a number permanently.
- [x] Unit and UI coverage compiles for multiple kinds and player colours.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- Name generation should derive from the selected player's saved plans at creation time rather than global mutable counters.
- Exact matching of the generated-name pattern should not treat unrelated user names as numbered defaults.

## Evidence

- Added a pure default-name generator derived from saved plans of the selected player and kind, choosing the first unused positive number.
- Exact generated-name matching leaves unrelated user-entered names alone; names remain freely editable and are only generated when creation begins.
- Added unit coverage for numbering gaps, plan kinds, player colours, and unrelated names, plus UI assertions for both initial defaults.
